WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Most people don't fail at selling

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.200
digital products because they're bad.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.880
They fail because of this. They try to

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.120
build a product first and then they try

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.120
and find people to sell it to. But this

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.040
is actually backwards. You can have the

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.360
best course, ebook, template, coaching

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.440
offer, Notion dashboard, or digital

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.880
download in the world. But if nobody's

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.000
looking for that solution and nobody

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.040
understands the value that this product

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.760
brings, then the truth is that it is

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.280
just going to sit there. So in this

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.400
video, I'm going to break down the

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.960
biggest reasons why most people fail at

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.480
selling digital products and more

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.040
importantly how to actually fix each

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.080
one. Because selling digital products

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.080
does not have to be complicated, but it

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.320
is definitely specific. So here's

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.280
usually what happens. People will go to

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.160
a place like YouTube and see a video

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.120
like this one talking about how to start

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.960
selling digital products. And they get

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.560
excited. I mean, I have fallen into this

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.800
trap myself as well. You then go on to

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.000
spend days, weeks, or maybe even months

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.040
curating the perfect digital product so

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.080
that you can start making $10,000 a

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.760
month. You go through design it, polish

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.840
it, make the sales page, set up a

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.839
checkout, maybe even create a logo, and

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.080
then you go ahead and launch it. And

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:09.000
then, wah wah wah, nothing happened.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.440
Maybe you get a few likes. Maybe you get

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.040
a friend who is nice enough to buy it.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.320
Maybe you get a little bit of traffic,

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.120
but you're not actually getting real

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.200
sales. So you assume that your product

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.160
is bad. But the reality is that a lot of

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.760
times that's not actually the issue. The

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.160
real issue is that you actually skipped

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.520
the parts that create demand, which is

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.600
kind of the most important thing when it

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.560
comes to actually selling digital

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.440
products. So let's go through the four

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.040
big mistakes. The first mistake is

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.880
building a product before you even have

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.640
an audience. Now, when I say an

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.800
audience, don't get scared off because

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.680
this does not mean that you have to

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.440
have, you know, 100,000 or a million

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.800
followers in order to start generating

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.560
sales from digital products. But what

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.600
you do need is some kind of proof that

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.040
people care about the problem that

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.880
you're solving. And the truth is that

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.960
most beginners actually skip this. They

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.640
create something based on what they

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.000
think people want instead of paying

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.240
attention to what people are already

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.200
asking for. So how do you do this? I I

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:59.200
the first and most important step is

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.040
actually to not just solve the problem,

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.680
but understand the pain point and where

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.320
the pain is coming from for this

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.040
specific problem. For example, let's say

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.600
you want to create a budgeting template.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.800
Now, that sounds fine and all, but

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.680
budgeting template is extremely broad.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.040
So, who's it for? Is it for college

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.080
students? Is it for new parents? Is it

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.880
for freelancers trying to generate

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.440
consistent income? Is it for people

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.880
trying to pay off debt? Or is it for

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.800
small business owners? These are all

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.560
very, very different types of people

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.880
that have different problems, different

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.160
pain points and are trying to actually

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.280
solve a different problem based on who

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.840
exactly you're targeting. For example,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.640
me as a new parent, I like to keep track

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.480
of our grocery spending expenses. This

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.000
may be significantly different from a

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.600
freelancer who's trying to figure out

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.280
their cash flow. So, as you can see with

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.120
this example, this is the same category,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.640
the same type of digital product, but

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.480
solving a very different problem based

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.160
on who you're trying to solve to. So,

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.959
your product should actually be a direct

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.520
response to that struggle. So, how do

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:54.040
you fix this? Before you build the

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.200
product, actually create content around

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.840
the problem. This can look like creating

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.000
short-form videos on TikTok, creating

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.080
long-form videos on YouTube, sending

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.560
emails, making carousel posts, or even

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.160
just starting conversations with the

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.680
people around you. Then, start paying

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.400
attention to things like what people are

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.959
asking you about, what the conversation

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.040
is directing towards, what types of

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.360
things get comments, saves, likes,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.920
shares, etc. In this scenario, you're

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.760
not necessarily just trying to grow an

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.400
audience, you're trying to understand

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.360
from your audience what is their

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.840
existing pain point and how can you

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.480
solve that. For me, on my YouTube

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.400
videos, I kept getting comments saying,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.959
"I would love you know, an e-guide or

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.280
some sort of digital download where you

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:31.160
walk through step-by-step how to

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.560
actually get monetized on YouTube." So,

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.280
that's where I created my Mom to

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.519
Monetize ebook. I already had people

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.320
asking me in my comments about this

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.239
specific problem, and then I went and

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.560
created a solution for those people. All

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:44.920
right, let's talk about mistake number

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.400
two, which is bad positioning. So, this

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.760
is where somebody actually does have a

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.400
really useful digital product, but they

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.920
don't explain it very well. They might

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.200
say things like, "I made a productivity

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.080
template. I created a fitness guide. I

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.800
made a course about marketing." Or "I

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.560
sell digital planners." But the problem

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.560
is that none of those tell you who

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.960
they're for or exactly what problem

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.320
they're solving. And generic items like

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:07.080
this are hard to sell because the

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.280
reality is the customer is going to say,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.560
"Well, why should I care? Why should I

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.920
buy your digital planner over that one?"

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.760
So again, this is why it's so important

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.200
to understand who your product is for,

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.280
what problem it solves, why it is

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.239
different, and what result they will get

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.680
from buying your digital product. So I

00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:21.680
have a simple formula that you can use

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.720
to better position your digital

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.560
products. Take who it is for, the

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.240
painful problem, and then the specific

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.280
outcome. For example, instead of saying

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.480
I sell a meal planning template, try

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.000
saying a 30-minute weekly meal planning

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:35.919
system for busy parents who are tired of

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.919
overspending on takeout. See how much

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:40.040
more specific that is? Or instead of I

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:42.120
made a budgeting spreadsheet, try a

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.880
simple budget tracker for freelancers to

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.160
manage consistent income without feeling

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.280
overwhelmed. You see the difference

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.000
here? The product is not actually

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.240
changing, it's just positioning and the

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.440
way that you're communicating it to your

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.160
customers. So the fix here is to stop

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.400
trying to sell to everyone because when

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.440
your product feels like it's for

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:58.640
everyone, it's actually for no one. Get

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.320
specific, pick the exact type of person

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.880
you're trying to solve a problem for,

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.280
and communicate what the result is that

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.680
they're going to get from your digital

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.400
product. The third mistake I often see

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.760
digital product creators making is not

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.320
having a distribution strategy. This is

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:13.120
actually a huge one. So most people will

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.880
spend 90% of their time actually

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.840
focusing on and building a really cool

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.600
digital product, and only 10% of the

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.200
time figuring out how they're going to

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.760
distribute it. But unfortunately, a

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.840
product is not going to sell just

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.720
because it exists. So you actually need

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.560
a system for getting your product to the

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:29.120
right people, not just once, but on a

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.960
consistent basis. That's how this

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.960
becomes a source of passive income that

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.520
does generate you those $10,000 a month

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.960
that you see people talking about on

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.400
YouTube. So here's what a simple

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.919
distribution plan can actually look

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.400
like. That system could start with

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:42.680
YouTube, but it could also start with

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.880
things like TikTok, Instagram, email,

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.160
SEO, partnerships. Whatever it is, it

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.840
doesn't matter, but there does have to

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.040
be some sort of strategy that you're

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.240
putting into to generate consistent

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.880
traffic and visibility on your product

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.120
over time. First, you'll create content

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.840
that actually talks about the pain

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.520
point, then you'll give people a quick

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.040
win so that they can trust you. For

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.920
example, let's say you're talking about

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.520
selling workout guides, maybe you share

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:06.160
that you actually lost 50 lb with your

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.160
own workout plans. And then lastly,

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.040
you'll want to actually show them the

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.880
product as the third step. So, here's a

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.040
few examples of how this could look. If

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.680
you're focusing on budgeting type of

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.040
niche, your content could look like "How

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.800
to budget when income changes every

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.600
single month? Three mistakes freelancers

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.600
make with money. How to stop underpaying

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.880
yourself as a freelancer. What I would

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:25.720
do if I had irregular income and no

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.240
budget." See how all of those content

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.280
ideas are related to the same problem

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.760
around making money and budgeting as a

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.360
freelancer, so that when you do

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.160
introduce your budgeting template for

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.919
freelancers, it actually flows and makes

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.600
sense. And the fourth mistake I often

00:06:35.919 --> 00:06:39.600
see people doing with digital products

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.800
is overcomplicating the product. This

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.800
happens all the time. You think of a

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.440
digital product and it can sound very

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.680
complex, very complicated. For example,

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:48.560
somebody might try and create a

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:50.560
12-module course, a 100-page ebook, a

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.360
50-tab spreadsheet, or an all-in-one

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:54.000
system. You might be creating a product

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:55.720
thinking that more is better because

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.280
it's solving more problems, but actually

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.560
this creates more friction for you, you

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.640
have to create more, you have to build

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.720
more, it's going to take you longer to

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:04.440
launch, and if I'm being quite honest

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.800
with you, a 50-tab budgeting spreadsheet

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.000
would actually be very intimidating and

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:10.160
overwhelming for me as a beginner. So,

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.280
sometimes simple is actually better. So

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.880
again, think of it like this. If

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.640
somebody is stressed, confused, looking

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:17.280
for help, they're usually not thinking,

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.560
"I want to buy this all-in-one that's

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.919
going to solve every problem I've ever

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.360
had." They're actually probably just

00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:22.840
thinking it very simply, "Can somebody

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.280
just help me with the next step and

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.120
figure out what to do?" This is where

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.480
simple products can actually sell really

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.600
well. Things like templates, checklists,

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:32.000
short ebooks, mini courses, etc. all

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.919
tend to do actually a lot better for

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.680
this very reason. So, the fix here is to

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:36.840
make the product simple and to create it

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.440
fast. So, when you're creating your

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.200
digital product, ask yourself, "How can

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.320
I make this easier? How can I help them

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.920
get the result faster? Or what is the

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:45.760
smallest product that I can create that

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:47.680
will still solve the problem. So, just a

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:49.040
recap, the reason a lot of people fail

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.720
is because they're starting with a

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.000
product, then they go and try to find an

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.440
audience, then they try to figure out

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.040
their positioning, then they go get

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.480
traffic, but they're better off actually

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.400
doing the opposite. Start with the

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:00.240
audience, find their pain point, create

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.000
content around that pain point, validate

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.200
the demand, and then create the simplest

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.640
product you can that solves the problem

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.600
for your audience. And that's actually

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.360
why I created a digital product starter

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:11.120
kit. It's designed for people who want

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:12.840
to get started selling digital products

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.760
without having to guess, overbuild, or

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.200
waste months on something that, frankly,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.919
nobody is going to buy. I walk you

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.360
through how to choose the right idea,

00:08:17.919 --> 00:08:21.280
position it clearly, validate your

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.880
demand, and create a simple product that

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:24.960
people actually want. So, that instead

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.640
of starting with a random product idea,

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.600
you start with a real problem, a real

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.080
buyer, and a simple path to starting to

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.240
get sales from digital products. I'll

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.919
have that linked down in my description

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.599
box. So, before you build your next

00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:35.880
digital product, remember this: Do not

00:08:34.599 --> 00:08:37.960
start with the product, start with the

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.560
person, find their pain, solve it

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:41.120
simply, and then build a system that

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.680
gets your solution in front of people on

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.200
a regular basis. If you guys found this

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.360
video useful and helpful, make sure you

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.360
hit that subscribe button. I love

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.560
sharing tips about selling digital

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:51.080
products, making money online, and more.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.720
So, if you like that type of content,

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.080
